      "head_commit": {
        "id": "dd7235cb6a55e9987551719ee57de9c3ff59d115",
        "tree_id": "6dd1f6b6e0f12bbf0ef79660b06a2f3b6d75151a",
        "message": "url: reduce search params sort buffering\n\nURLSearchParams.sort() copies both merge runs into temporary arrays.\nBuffer only the left run and read the right run from the output array,\nremoving one scratch-array allocation and the right-run copying.\n\nWhile left-side elements remain, the output cursor stays behind unread\nright-side elements. Once the left run is exhausted, the right remainder\nis already in place. Taking the left key on equality preserves\nstability. The insertion-sort path below 50 pairs is unchanged.\n\nSigned-off-by: Roberto Bianchi <roberto.bianchi@spendesk.com>\nPR-URL: https://github.com/nodejs/node/pull/66665\nReviewed-By: Xuguang Mei <meixuguang@gmail.com>\nReviewed-By: Matteo Collina <matteo.collina@gmail.com>\nReviewed-By: Ilyas Shabi <ilyasshabi94@gmail.com>\nReviewed-By: Gürgün Dayıoğlu <hey@gurgun.day>",
        "timestamp": "2026-10-14T08:51:58Z",
